   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 7. Unclassifiable Vehicles (Klasse 6 and Klasse 250)\n",
    "\n",
    "Two classification codes indicate problematic records:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Klasse 6** (`nk Kfz` — nicht klassifizierbar): the sensor could not classify the vehicle.\n",
    "  A high rate per sensor suggests an alignment or obstruction problem.\n",
    "- **Klasse 250 (partially obscured)** (`Kfz`)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 129,
   "id": "10fc09c7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Klasse 6 / 250 (unclassifiable, row-level): 86 rows\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "UNCLASSIFIABLE_CODES = {6, 250}   # row-level unclassifiable\n",
    "\n",
    "df[\"flag_unclassifiable\"]   = df[\"klasse\"].isin(UNCLASSIFIABLE_CODES)\n",
    "n_unclass  = df[\"flag_unclassifiable\"].sum()\n",
    "qa_report[\"unclassifiable_rows\"]    = int(n_unclass)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Klasse 6 / 250 (unclassifiable, row-level): {n_unclass:,} rows\")"
   ]
  },
